<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed stronger at 3.02 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed stronger at 3.02 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.0580 to the dollar, down from 3.0565 on Thursday and at 1.8075 to the mark, up from 1.8090, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 3.02 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Thursday's 2.88 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
